---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { withBase } from "../lib/base";
---

<Base title="Support · AutoLog" description="Connecting your car, recording a drive, and knowing where your data goes.">
  <article class="reading-page">
    <header class="introduction">
      <p class="eyebrow">Support</p>
      <h1>A little help,<br />and you’re off.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Connecting your car, recording a drive, and knowing where your data goes.</p>
    </header>
    <section><h2>Which adapters work?</h2><p>Use a compatible Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) ELM327 adapter. Classic Bluetooth and Wi-Fi-only adapters aren’t supported.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Why does the first connection take a while?</h2><p>Some older cars use a slower protocol. The adapter tries the available protocols until the car answers. Give the first connection time to finish before trying again.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Does AutoLog clear fault codes?</h2><p>No. AutoLog reads live data and reports the faults it sees. It never clears a code or writes anything to the car.</p></section>
    <section><h2>What about EVs and hybrids?</h2><p>AutoLog uses the signals your car provides. A hybrid keeps its engine-off miles; an EV gets a display without fuel calculations. Available readings vary by car.</p></section>
    <section><h2>What if I’m parking for a while?</h2><p>Power draw depends on your adapter and car. Follow your adapter maker’s storage guidance and unplug the adapter for extended parking.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Where does my data live?</h2><p>On your phone. No account, no AutoLog server, and no analytics. VIN decoding and road-geometry lookups use external services; the <a href={withBase("/privacy")}>Privacy page</a> explains them.</p></section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .introduction { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; }
  .eyebrow { font-size: 15px; }
  h1 { font-size: 68px; line-height: 72px; }
  .lede { font-size: 18px; line-height: 28px; }
  section { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; padding-top: 24px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  h2 { font-size: 30px; line-height: 36px; }
  section p { font-size: 17px; line-height: 27px; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    h1 { font-size: 44px; line-height: 48px; }
    h2 { font-size: 26px; line-height: 31px; }
  }
</style>
